  <prompt>Apply punch row A41 from `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` (auth-v4 §10.1 Δ5 + §10.4 dual Dataverse app-user + Q8 owner disposition 2026-08-25). Row-by-row execution: (a) DEDUPE FIRST against in-flight `Wave-3E-053-H10-AppUser` + `ds8-uami-dv-appuser` landed output — grep + read what those agents produced BEFORE editing H10 handler. If both app-user rows already created, scope collapses to probe-only (−2h). (b) READ T2 probe (`E2EAcceptance/T2*Probe.cs`) BEFORE extending — the "count-only" assumption is UNCONFIRMED per remediation plan §5 SF-9 (inferred from test messages "OK (count=1)"/"COUNT=0"); if probe already does byte-equality, mark A41 partial-already-applied on that dimension. (c) Ensure H10 handler creates BOTH app-user rows per environment: (1) app-reg row (OBO path — token appid stays the app-reg under MI-FIC); (2) UAMI row with `applicationid = UAMI clientId` AND **`azureactivedirectoryobjectid = UAMI principalId` (NOT clientId — the silent-fail trap; app-only DV 401s otherwise; auth-v4 "single most-missed item")**. (d) Extend T2 probe with the principalId byte-equality assertion. (e) Assert Model 1 code path: shared app-reg SP + shared UAMI once per DV env, zero per-customer app-reg objects (Section 5.1 Reading 1). (f) Assert Model 2 code path: per-customer app-reg + per-stamp UAMI. (g) Fix `design.md:153` figure drift ("10/14 GUIDs null" → GraphAppRoles.cs is source of truth; count reflects 11 null + 3 filled = 14 total, will become 15 after task 203c A16 completes). (h) Q8 (a): fix `design.md:61` D3 wording drift — replace "Managed Identity" in Model 1 "per-customer dedicated" list with an explicit shared-UAMI clause referencing task-029 slot-swap fix + I6 code-level isolation. (i) Q8 (b): add a Model 1 UAMI row to the Naming Standards table (`design.md:~658`) for `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami` alongside the existing Model 2 `mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{env}` row. (j) Update runbook `docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md` Section 12 with dual-row + trap-recognition + recovery recipe. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE L2 provisioning platform + Dataverse app-user expert + auth-v4 integration specialist. Expert in: H10 `EnsureDataverseAppUserHandler` semantics (dual app-user rows per environment: app-reg for OBO, UAMI for app-only calls); the §10.4 objectid trap (UAMI row's `azureactivedirectoryobjectid` MUST equal UAMI principalId, NOT clientId — silent-fail; app-only DV 401s otherwise; per auth-v4 `mi-proof-dataverse-side.md`); T2 probe (`E2EAcceptance/T2*Probe.cs`) assertion patterns and Dataverse `systemuser` alt-key resolution; Model 1 vs Model 2 tenancy shape (Model 1 Reading 1 = one shared multitenant app-reg + one shared UAMI per DV env, zero per-customer app-reg objects; Model 2 = per-customer app-reg + per-stamp UAMI); design.md D3 tenancy narrative (spec.md:253 v3.5 MUST split, R23 CLOSED, I6 code-level isolation per FR-40, task-029 slot-swap fix); GraphAppRoles.cs 14-slot contract (source of truth for the design.md:153 figure); dedupe protocol against in-flight parallel agents.</role>

  <goal>Row A41 annotated with `last_known_status_after_execution` in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` (or its integrated location in `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` if merged). H10 handler creates BOTH app-user rows per environment (or dedupe output already does, in which case A41 scope collapses to probe-only with −2h effort reduction noted in task summary). T2 probe (`E2EAcceptance/T2*Probe.cs`) extended with the principalId byte-equality assertion — READ the probe FIRST; extend based on its actual current assertions (do NOT assume "count-only" per §5 SF-9 caveat). Model 1 code path asserted: shared app-reg SP + shared UAMI once per DV env, zero per-customer app-reg objects (Reading 1). Model 2 code path asserted: per-customer app-reg + per-stamp UAMI. `design.md:61` D3 wording fixed per Q8 (a) draft edit — "Managed Identity" in Model 1 per-customer-dedicated list replaced with explicit shared-UAMI clause referencing task-029 slot-swap fix + I6 code-level isolation (per remediation plan §3.1). `design.md:~658` Naming Standards table has a Model 1 UAMI row for `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami` alongside the existing Model 2 `mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{env}` row (Q8 (b)). `design.md:153` figure drift fixed: GraphAppRoles.cs cited as source of truth (11 null + 3 filled = 14 total; will become 15 after task 203c A16 completes). Runbook `docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md` Section 12 documents dual-row contract + trap-recognition symptom (app-only DV 401 with row EXISTS + passes count-check) + recovery recipe (repair `azureactivedirectoryobjectid` from clientId to principalId). Integration test: post-H10, both app-user rows exist AND T2 probe passes with byte-equality assertion. `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` succeeds (no BFF publish-size delta expected — A41 does not touch BFF-consumed shared code).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Auth-v4 §10.1 Δ5 + §10.4 identify the dual Dataverse app-user contract as "auth-v4's single most-missed item": every environment needs TWO `systemuser` rows — (1) an app-reg row (for OBO tokens where the `appid` claim is the app-reg), and (2) a UAMI row (for app-only calls where the token is minted for the UAMI). The trap that survived three prior audits: the UAMI row's `azureactivedirectoryobjectid` field MUST hold the UAMI's **principalId (objectId)**, NOT its clientId. Both are valid-shaped GUIDs; both create a row that passes existence + count checks; only the app-only Dataverse call at first use returns 401 (Dataverse expects the token subject's objectId to match the row's `azureactivedirectoryobjectid`). Design intent is present at `design.md:153` (H10 "BFF app-reg + UAMI") but execution was deferred to a downstream row. In-flight parallel agents `Wave-3E-053-H10-AppUser` and `ds8-uami-dv-appuser` are producing pieces of this contract — A41 dedupes against their output FIRST and only extends where gaps remain. T2 probe (task 177 landed) verifies app-user existence but the current assertion shape is UNCONFIRMED per remediation plan §5 SF-9 (test message fragments "OK (count=1)"/"COUNT=0" suggest count-only, but this was never verified by direct read); A41 requires READING the probe before extending it. Q8 owner disposition 2026-08-25 extended A41 (+0.5h) to also fix two design.md drifts adjacent to the H10 contract: (a) `design.md:61` D3 wording that still lists "Managed Identity" as per-customer dedicated for Model 1 (stale — predates v3.5 auth-v4 MI-FIC coordination which established the single shared `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami`; per remediation plan §3.1 the shared-UAMI + I6 clause is authoritative); (b) `design.md:~658` Naming Standards table currently has only Model 2 `mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{env}` — adding a Model 1 row for `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami` prevents future drift by making the pattern explicit in the naming registry. §6.5 resolution record (`notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md`) APPROVED 2026-08-25 provides the authoritative auth-v4 context (Amendment A4 + E-3 closure + Model 1/2 topology). This row does NOT touch BFF-consumed shared code (`src/server/shared/**` untouched) → no NFR-01 publish-size verification required. Row A41 is BLOCKS-186 (auth-v4 Section 10.1 Δ5 + Section 10.4 dual app-user trap) — task 186 E2E live-fire is gated on A41 landing.</background>
