  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, high effort, sonnet tier). Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` row A41 (full text) + `notes/auth-v4-integration-remediation-plan.md` §3.1/§3.2/§5/§7 + `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` §Owner-refinements + `notes/auth-v4-integration-open-questions.md` Q8 disposition. Read `design.md:55-65` (D3 area), `:150-160` (H10 area), `:650-670` (Naming Standards table area).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep + resolve target file paths">Grep-locate the actual H10 handler file (candidates: `src/server/**/Handlers/**/H10*.cs`, `src/server/**/Handlers/**/EnsureDataverseAppUserHandler.cs`, `src/server/**/L2/**/H10*.cs`). Grep-locate the actual T2 probe file (`tests/**/E2EAcceptance/T2*.cs` or similar). Record verified paths in scratchpad. Verify H10 handler does NOT reside in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — if it does, STOP and re-scope for BFF publish-size obligation.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Dedupe FIRST against in-flight agents (BINDING)">Grep + read `Wave-3E-053-H10-AppUser` + `ds8-uami-dv-appuser` landed output (look in `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/wave-3e-053-h10-appuser-*.md` + `notes/design-study-ds8-uami-dv-appuser-*.md` + recent commit log for `Wave-3E-053` or `ds8` tags). Determine EXACTLY which pieces of the dual-row contract are already landed vs still gapped. Record dedupe verdict in scratchpad. If BOTH app-user rows already created by dedupe output, MARK A41 scope-collapse-to-probe-only + note the −2h effort reduction.</step>
    <step order="3" name="READ T2 probe BEFORE extending (BINDING §5 SF-9 caveat)">Read the full T2 probe file identified in Step 1. Determine EXACT current assertion shape (count-only vs already byte-equality vs something else). Do NOT assume "count-only" per §5 SF-9 caveat. Record actual assertions in scratchpad. If probe already does byte-equality on `azureactivedirectoryobjectid == UAMI principalId`, MARK A41 partial-already-applied on the probe-extension dimension.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint (after 4 discovery steps)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "Checkpoint."). Emit dedupe + probe-read verdict summary as a scratchpad table so downstream steps have a clear baseline.</step>
    <step order="5" name="H10 handler dual-row apply (conditional on dedupe verdict)">IF dedupe covered BOTH app-user rows: skip; annotate A41 as probe-only scope. OTHERWISE: EDIT H10 handler to create BOTH rows per environment: (a) app-reg row (`applicationid = app-reg clientId`, `azureactivedirectoryobjectid = app-reg SP objectId`); (b) UAMI row (`applicationid = UAMI clientId`, `azureactivedirectoryobjectid = UAMI principalId (objectId) — NOT clientId`). Model 1 branch: register SHARED app-reg SP + shared UAMI once per DV env, ZERO per-customer app-reg objects (Reading 1). Model 2 branch: per-customer app-reg + per-stamp UAMI. Cite auth-v4 §10.4 in handler comment + reference `mi-proof-dataverse-side.md` for the trap.</step>
    <step order="6" name="T2 probe byte-equality extension (conditional on probe-read)">IF probe already does byte-equality: skip. OTHERWISE: EDIT T2 probe to assert `azureactivedirectoryobjectid == expected UAMI principalId` (byte-for-byte, NOT just count). Test message MUST distinguish "OK (byte-equality verified)" from "OK (count only — DEGRADED)" so future readers can tell whether the byte-equality assertion actually ran. Add a negative test case: probe FAILS LOUD when `azureactivedirectoryobjectid` holds the UAMI clientId instead of principalId (the trap).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Checkpoint (after 2 code edits)">Run `context-handoff`.</step>
    <step order="8" name="design.md:153 figure drift fix">EDIT `design.md:153` H10 row: replace the stale "10/14 GUIDs null" text with "GraphAppRoles.cs is source of truth (currently 11 null + 3 filled = 14 total; becomes 15 total after task 203c A16 completes)". Also add per-model identity sources: Model 1 = "shared app-reg appId + shared UAMI, `azureactivedirectoryobjectid = principalId`"; Model 2 = "per-customer app-reg + stamp UAMI, `azureactivedirectoryobjectid = stamp UAMI principalId`" (per remediation plan §3.3 cascade item 3).</step>
    <step order="9" name="Q8 (a) — design.md:61 D3 wording fix">Re-read `design.md:61` D3 to catch any post-2026-08-25 drift. If further drifted, reconcile with latest before applying Q8 (a). EDIT: replace "Managed Identity" in D3's Model 1 "per-customer dedicated" list with an explicit shared-UAMI clause: "In Model 1, the BFF Managed Identity is a SINGLE shared `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami` per environment (NOT per-customer), coordinated per auth-v4 MI-FIC contract (Amendment A4); per-customer isolation is code-level via invariant I6 (see FR-40 + task 130) and slot-persistence-safe per task-029 slot-swap fix."</step>
    <step order="10" name="Q8 (b) — Naming Standards table Model 1 UAMI row">Re-read `design.md:~658` Naming Standards table area. Confirm Model 2 row for `mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{env}` present (per remediation plan assumption). If ABSENT, STOP + escalate — the whole table needs review, not a single-row add. Otherwise: ADD a Model 1 row for `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami` alongside the Model 2 row. Row cells: {Resource type: "Managed Identity (UAMI)", Model: "Model 1", Naming pattern: `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami`, Scope: "shared per DV environment (zero per-customer)", Source of truth: "§6.5 resolution record 2026-08-25 + FR-40 I6", Notes: "coordinated with auth-v4 MI-FIC; slot-persistence-safe per task-029 slot-swap fix"}.</step>
    <step order="11" name="Runbook Section 12 dual-row + trap-recognition + recovery">EDIT `docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md` Section 12: document dual-row contract (app-reg row for OBO + UAMI row for app-only); trap-recognition symptom (app-only DV 401 with row EXISTS + passes count-check → check `azureactivedirectoryobjectid` byte-equals UAMI principalId, NOT clientId); recovery recipe (repair the row via Web API PATCH: `PATCH /systemusers({rowId}) { azureactivedirectoryobjectid: '{UAMI principalId GUID}' }`); reference to auth-v4 §10.4 + T2 probe test-case. MUST NOT reintroduce the retired never-delete rationale per §6.5 resolution.</step>
