  <notes>Justification (root CLAUDE.md §11 three-question template): **Existing** — A41 EXTENDS existing H10 handler + T2 probe (task 177 landed) + design.md D3 narrative + Naming Standards table + runbook Section 12 (docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md). No NEW files created (the row is entirely modifications to existing surfaces; if dedupe reveals a NEW file must be created, §11 obligation applies to that file specifically). **Extension** — A41 extends existing components rather than creating new ones: (a) the H10 handler gets a UAMI branch alongside its existing app-reg row creation logic; (b) T2 probe gets a byte-equality assertion alongside its existing existence check; (c) design.md D3 + Naming Standards table + `:153` figure each get single-clause edits; (d) runbook Section 12 gets a subsection append. No new services, abstractions, endpoints, or file surfaces. **Cost-of-doing-nothing** — auth-v4 §10.4 documents this as "the single most-missed item"; per remediation plan §5 SF-9 the concrete failure mode is: silent 401s on EVERY app-only Dataverse call post-cutover, with rows that EXIST and pass count-checks. Task 186 E2E live-fire is BLOCKED on A41 landing (per punch row A-blocks-E2E YES section). Without Q8 (a), design.md D3 continues to teach the retired Model 1 per-customer-MI narrative — the exact "knowledge-file drift on auth" failure class per SF-21. Without Q8 (b), the shared-UAMI Model 1 pattern is not in the Naming Standards registry — future rows will re-drift by omission. Costs are concrete + measurable, not "abstraction layer / future flexibility".

Blast radius: H10 handler + T2 probe (auth-tagged; test-modifying override → FULL rigor + unconditional code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 per root §8). Model tier: Sonnet-5 @ high per remediation plan §8 cost posture (A38 + A42 are the Fable/Opus rows for credential-logic + cross-worktree consumption; A41 is mechanical apply of a well-specified delta). No NFR-01 publish-size verification required (A41 does not touch BFF-consumed shared code). Depends on A35 (landed) + dedupe review of two in-flight parallel agents. Effort 3.5h estimated (may drop to 1.5h if dedupe collapses to probe-only per punch row A41 effort annotation + owner-review checklist item).</notes>

